sections.concept:
The **Fundamental Review of the Trading Book (FRTB)** is the Basel Committee's overhaul of
market-risk capital, finalised in January 2019 and consolidated into the MAR standard with an
implementation date of 1 January 2023 (national timelines differ). It replaced the Basel II /
Basel 2.5 rules with:

- a revised **trading book boundary** (RBC25);
- a new, risk-sensitive **Standardised Approach** built on sensitivities (MAR20–23);
- an **Internal Models Approach** based on Expected Shortfall with liquidity horizons,
  approved **desk by desk** and subject to tougher tests (MAR30–33);
- a **capital floor and fallback**: every bank computes the SA, and desks failing IMA
  tests fall back to it.
